= a[1] =2. Also from sequences ending run2 at n-1? but b[1]=0. So a[2]=2, b[2]=2. S2=4.\n\nNow recurrence for n>=3:\na[n] = number of sequences length n ending with run length1. This can come from sequences length n-1 ending with run length1 or run length2, by adding opposite bit. So a[n] = a[n-1] + b[n-1].\nb[n] = number ending with run length2. This can only come from sequences length n-1 ending with run length1, by adding same bit. So b[n] = a[n-1].\n\nThus recurrence:\na[n] = a[n-1] + b[n-1]\nb[n] = a[n-1]\nSo we can compute.\n\nLet's compute up to n=12.\n\nInitialize:\nn=1: a1=2, b1=0\nn=2: a2=2, b2=2\nn=3:\na3 = a2 + b2 = 2+2"}}],"created":1790984579,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4879,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-DzkO0trRuLhIeqqIbjCVY5rC0AbX2Tnx","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4111,"prompt_ms":502.055,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12212478715640963,"prompt_per_second":8188.34589835775,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2347.838,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.061066492829205,"predicted_per_second":326.6835275687675}}